From b2ce036a670a9b3657d2342eadf4a6949275601c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Zhou <alex.zhou@edge0.ai>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:36:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] moe_pool v4: full engine-parity pool (staging queues,
 pin, blob, trim, metrics)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Feature parity with the mainline engine's streaming/expert_pool, landed item by item:
- equal-size slot state machine EMPTY/LOADING/READY/FAILED + IO-thread queue (E0_IO_THREADS, default 4)
- dual queues: the demand-dedicated queue pops first (mixed FIFO was confirmed to suffer prefetch
  head-of-line blocking -- the 14s/token pseudo-hang incident)
- pin protocol: slots in compute are unevictable; released wholesale at the next ensure entry
  (barrier quiescence contract)
- acquire hitting LOADING waits on a cv + FAILED falls back synchronously (stall_ms metered, ~ the
  engine's acq metric)
- resident blob: one copy-in per non-expert mmap-view tensor (E0_BLOB_MB, isomorphic to the engine's
  img mirror)
- watermark trim E0_MEM_FLOOR_MB (when MemAvailable drops below the line, evict non-pinned READY
  down to 60%)
- metrics aligned with the engine's PoolMetrics: hits/misses/stall/pf_issued-used-waste-drop-miss/flash/evicts/trims
- prefetch K=4->8 (teacher n_ids=8 evidences 35b top-8) + throttled drop when the main queue backs up >64
- registration point moved: tensors at the tail of load_tensors have data=NULL (ml.contexts copies),
  so llama_model_load now calls llama_model::moe_wire() after load_tensors (tensors_by_name primary
  set, virtual-interface hook)
- registered fds are always dup()'d (hang incident: pread got EBADF after the loader closed the original fd)
- find_tp matches by name + self-corrects the pointer (graph-copy pointers != load-set pointers)

Known differences from the engine (on record): the worker head math is the scalar version (NEON
queued); trim does no physical tail-block release (the bump arena's middle is not contiguous);
prep-slot tail pre-conversion is N/A (llama dequantizes ad hoc).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
